Description: hog-lib: enable notifications even when the CCC cannot be read
 The HUAWEI MatePad Keyboard (12d1:10b2) answers the read of its Input
 Report's Client Characteristic Configuration with "Read Not Permitted".
 hog-lib then skipped enabling notifications and, because that failed
 request was the last pending one, never read the Report Map either, so no
 uhid device was created: the keyboard paired and connected but typed
 nothing.  Write the CCC regardless and carry on.
Author: Linux 7.0 MatePad port
--- a/profiles/input/hog-lib.c
+++ b/profiles/input/hog-lib.c
@@ -433,15 +433,14 @@
 	struct gatt_request *req = user_data;
 	struct report *report = req->user_data;
 
-	if (status != 0) {
-		error("Error reading CCC value: %s", att_ecode2str(status));
-		goto remove;
-	}
+	if (status != 0)
+		error("Error reading CCC value: %s (enabling notifications anyway)",
+						att_ecode2str(status));
 
 	write_ccc(report->hog, report->hog->attrib, report->ccc_handle, report);
 
-remove:
-	remove_gatt_req(req, status);
+	/* The CCC write is queued now; let it decide when the map is read. */
+	remove_gatt_req(req, 0);
 }
 
 static const char *type_to_string(uint8_t type)
